  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/84c0TXNZua3KytwpqFsRxx4EDqXFv1GLPTkSjLx_xqo.original.fullsize.png\">\nPoint of intersection of all curves is $(2,2 \\sqrt{2})$\nArea $=\\mathrm{A}_1+\\mathrm{A}_2$\n$\\alpha \\sqrt{2}=\\int_0^2 2 \\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}} \\mathrm{dx}+\\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\times 2 \\sqrt{2}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\alpha \\sqrt{2}=2\\left[\\frac{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right]_0^2+3 \\sqrt{2} \\\\ & \\alpha \\sqrt{2}=\\frac{17 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ & \\alpha=\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
